{"id":"granicus-68-337","platform":"granicus","body":"City Council","name":"CITY COUNCIL REGULAR","date":"2005-05-10","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://irvine.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=68&clip_id=337","minutes_url":"https://irvine.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?view_id=68&clip_id=337&doc_id=4f5a76d3-ed84-4691-ad13-88444c05e741","packet_url":"","clip_id":337,"view_id":68,"video_url":"https://irvine.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=68&clip_id=337","transcript_url":"","mp4_url":"https://archive-video.granicus.com/irvine/irvine_8bb75cd9c865dbee12132ef4daf954f5.mp4","mp3_url":"","agenda_text":"CITY COUNCIL AGENDA\n  BETH KROM\n  Mayor\n  SUKHEE KANG  LARRY AGRAN\n  Mayor Pro Tempore  Councilmember\n  STEVEN CHOI  CHRISTINA SHEA\n  Councilmember  Councilmember\n\n  CITY COUNCIL REGULAR\n  MEETING\n  May 10, 2005\n  4:00 P.M.\n  City Council Chamber\n  One Civic Center Plaza\n  NOTICE TO THE PUBLIC\n\nAt 11:00 p.m., the City Council will determine which of the remaining agenda items can be considered and acted\nupon prior to 12:00 midnight and will continue all other items on which additional time is required until a future City\nCouncil meeting. All meetings are scheduled to terminate at 12:00 midnight.\n\nADDITIONS AND DELETIONS TO THE AGENDA: Additions to the agenda are limited by California Government\nCode Section 54954.2 of the Brown Act and for those items that arise after the posting of the Agenda and must\nbe acted upon prior to the next City Council meeting.\n\nANNOUNCEMENTS/COMMITTEE REPORTS/COUNCIL COMMENTS: Announcements, Committee Reports\nand Council Comments are for the purpose of presenting brief comments or reports, are subject to California\nGovernment Code Section 54954.2 of the Brown Act and are limited to 15-minutes per meeting.\n\nCONSENT CALENDAR ITEMS: All matters listed under Consent Calendar are considered to be routine and all\nwill be enacted by one roll call vote. There will be no discussion of these items unless members of the City\nCouncil request specific items to be removed from the Consent Calendar for separate discussion. Any member of\nthe public may address the Council on items on the Consent Calendar. Public comments on any item or items on\nthe consent calendar are limited to three minutes per speaker. If you wish to speak to a particular item or items,\nplease complete a Speaker’s Form and give it to the City Clerk. (Please see information in “Request to Speak”\nsection.\n\nPUBLIC COMMENT: Any member of the public may address the City Council on items within the Council’s\nsubject matter jurisdiction but which are not listed on this agenda during public comments. However, no action\nmay be taken on matters that are not part of the posted agenda. Public comments are scheduled for 30 minutes\nand are limited to three minutes per person. If you wish to speak, please complete a Speaker’s Form and submit\nto the City Clerk.\n\fCITY COUNCIL – NOTICE TO THE PUBLIC\n\nSPEAKER’S CARD/REQUEST TO SPEAK: If you would like to address the City Council on a scheduled agenda\nitem, please complete the speaker’s card. The card is at the table at the entrance to the Council Chamber. Please\nidentify on the card your name, address, and the item on which you would like to speak and return to the City\nClerk. The speaker’s card assists the Mayor in ensuring that all persons wishing to address the Council are\nrecognized. Your name will be called at the time the matter is heard by the Council.\n\nSTAFF REPORTS: As a general rule, staff reports or other written documentation have been prepared or\norganized with respect to each item of business listed on the agenda. Copies of these materials are on file with\nthe City Clerk and are available for public inspection and copying. If you have any questions regarding any item of\nbusiness on the agenda for this meeting, or any of the staff reports or other documentation relating to any agenda\nitem, please contact City Clerk staff at (949) 724-6205.\n\nPUBLIC HEARINGS: Public Hearings are scheduled for a time certain of 4:00 p.m. (unless noticed otherwise) or\nas soon thereafter as possible. City Council, when considering the matter scheduled for hearing, will take the\nfollowing actions: 1) Open the Public Hearing. 2) Receive staff report. 3) Accept public testimony. 4) City Council\ncomments and questions. 5) Take appropriate action. Those wishing to address the City Council during the Public\nHearing must complete a “Request to Speak” form and provide it to the City Clerk prior to the hearing. If, in the\nfuture, you wish to challenge in court any of the matters on this agenda for which a public hearing is to be\nconducted, you may be limited to raising only those issues which you (or someone else) raised orally at the public\nhearing or in written correspondence received by the City at or before the hearing. Any person seeking to\nchallenge a City Council decision made as a result of a proceeding in which by law a hearing is required to be\ngiven, evidence is required to be taken, and the discretion in the determination of facts is vested in the City\nCouncil, shall be required to commence that action 90 days following the date on which the decision becomes\nfinal as provided in Code of Civil Procedure Section 1094.6. Please refer to Code of Civil Procedure 1094.6 to\ndetermine how to calculate when a decision becomes “final.” Notice: Public Hearings listed for continuance will\nbe continued as noted and posting of this agenda serves as notice of continuation. Any matter not noted for\ncontinuance, will be posted separately.\n\nAMERICANS WITH DISABILITIES ACT: It is the intention of the City of Irvine to comply with the Americans With\nDisabilities Act (ADA) in all respects. If, as an attendee or a participant at this meeting, you will need special\nassistance beyond what is normally provided, the City of Irvine will attempt to accommodate you in every\nreasonable manner. Please contact Jeri L. Stately, City Clerk, at least 48 hours prior to the meeting to inform us\nof your particular needs and to determine if accommodation is feasible. Please advise us at the time if you will\nneed accommodations to attend or participate in meetings on a regular basis.\n\nThis agenda was prepared by the City Clerk. Regular meetings of the City Council are held on the second and\nfourth Tuesdays of each month at 4:00 p.m. However, study sessions and/or closed sessions are periodically\nheld prior to the start of the regular meeting. The City Council Agenda is posted in the Police Department and\navailable at your local library. It is also available through our FAX LIBRARY system. Simply dial (949) 724-6210\nand request document number 100 anytime after 5:00 p.m. on the Friday prior to a City Council meeting. The\nAgenda may also be accessed through the City’s web page at www.ci.irvine.ca.us\n\n  STATE OF CALIFORNIA  )\n  CITY OF IRVINE  ) SS\n  COUNTY OF ORANGE  )\n\n  I DECLARE UNDER PENALTY OF PERJURY that I am employed by the City of Irvine, in\n  the City Clerk’s Department; and that I posted this agenda in the posting book located in\n  the Public Safety Lobby of City Hall, One Civic Center Plaza.\n\n  Dated/Signed: ___________________________________________________________\n\n  ii\n\f  FINAL\n  AGENDA\n\n  IRVINE\n  CITY COUNCIL\n  REGULAR MEETING\n\n  May 10, 2005\n\n  NOTICE TO THE PUBLIC\n\n  At 11:00 p.m., the City Council will determine which of the\n  remaining agenda items can be considered and acted upon\n  prior to 12:00 midnight and will continue all other items on\n  which additional time is required until a future City Council\n  meeting. All meetings are scheduled to terminate at 12:00\n  midnight.\n\nCALL TO ORDER  4:00 P.M.\n\nA regular meeting of the Irvine City Council will be called to order on May 10, 2005 at\n4:00 p.m., in the City Council Chamber, Irvine Civic Center, One Civic Center Plaza,\nIrvine, California, by Mayor Krom, presiding officer.\n\nROLL CALL\n\n  COUNCILMEMBER:  LARRY AGRAN\n  COUNCILMEMBER:  STEVEN CHOI\n  COUNCILMEMBER:  CHRISTINA SHEA\n  MAYOR PRO TEMPORE:  SUKHEE KANG\n  MAYOR:  BETH KROM\n\n********CONVENE TO THE IRVINE REDEVELOPMENT AGENCY MEETING********\n\nPlease see Irvine Redevelopment Agency Agenda.\n\n  1\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n******************RECONVENE TO THE CITY COUNCIL MEETING ******************\n\n**************PRESENTATIONS//WORKSHOPS/SCOPING SESSIONS**************\n\nPRESENTATION: TUSTIN UNIFIED SCHOOL DISTRICT - SUPERINTENDENT\nPETER C. GORMAN, Ed. D.\n\nSCOPING SESSION: PLANNING AREAS 1, 2, AND 9B (Submitted by Community\nDevelopment/Planning Services)\n\n***********************************************RECESS******************************************\n\n************RECONVENE TO THE CITY COUNCIL MEETING - 5:00 P.M.************\n\nPLEDGE OF ALLEGIANCE\n\nMOMENT OF SILENCE\n\nMayor Krom will request the City Council meeting be adjourned in memory of\nTherese Jane Francke.\n\nMUSICAL PRESENTATION\n\nThe University High School Sax Quartet will perform \"Luxury Lane\" by Carl\nFrangkiser and the Clarinet Quartet will perform \"Chicago\" by Fred Fisher.\n\nPRESENTATIONS\n\nProclamation on National Public Works Week - May 15-21, 2005\n\nINTRODUCTIONS\n\n*ANNOUNCEMENTS/COMMITTEE REPORTS/COUNCIL REPORTS\n\n*ADDITIONS AND DELETIONS\n\n*****************CONSENT CALENDAR (Item Nos. 1 through 5.1 )******************\n\n*PUBLIC COMMENTS (Limited to three (3) minutes per speaker)\n\n1.CITY COUNCIL MINUTES\n\n  1.1 APPROVAL OF CITY COUNCIL MINUTES (Submitted by City Clerk)\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  2\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n  ACTION:  Approve the minutes of a special meeting of the City\n  Council held on April 26, 2005.\n\n2.PROCLAMATIONS/COMMENDATIONS/RATIFICATIONS\n\n  2.1 PROCLAIM THE FOLLOWING:\n\n  1) Taiwanese American Heritage Week - May 16-22, 2005\n\n  2) National Public Works Week - May 15-21, 2005\n\n  2.2 COMMEND THE FOLLOWING:\n\n  1) Ralph J. Cicerone, Retiring Chancellor, University of California, Irvine,\n  1998-2005\n\n3.AGREEMENTS\n\n  3.1 RENEW LICENSE AGREEMENT WITH SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA EDISON\n  FOR BIKE TRAIL/PEDESTRIAN ACCESS AND LANDSCAPING\n  PURPOSES, WEST OF SAND CANYON AVENUE, NORTH OF BARRANCA\n  PARKWAY (PLANNING AREA 12, OAK CREEK) (Submitted by Public\n  Works/Development Engineering)\n\n  ACTION:  Approve License Agreement Account Number 2217 between\n  the City of Irvine and Southern California Edison, and authorize the Mayor\n  to execute and the City Clerk to attest said agreement, subject to the City\n  Attorney approval as to form.\n\n  3.2 APPROVAL OF MAP, BONDS, AND AGREEMENTS FOR TRACT MAP NO.\n  16779 (A PORTION OF VESTING TENTATIVE TRACT MAP NO. 16562)\n  (PLANNING AREA 6, PORTOLA SPRINGS) (Submitted by Public\n  Works/Development Engineering)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Approve Tract Map No. 16779.\n\n  2) Approve the agreements and accept the security from Pardee Homes,\n  Irvine Community Development Company LLC, and Standard Pacific\n  Corporation, guaranteeing improvements for Tract Map No. 16779.\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  3\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n  3) Authorize the Mayor to sign the agreements and the City Clerk to attest to\n  the agreements subject to City Attorney approval as to form.\n\n  4) Accept the dedication of an easement for public street and public utility\n  purposes within Tract Map No. 16779 for the following street right-of-way:\n  Arrowhead, Autumn Sage, Barley, Canoe, Conservancy, Deer Track,\n  Distant Star, Exploration, Gray Dove, Jackrabbit, Jasper, Land Grant,\n  Landbird, Los Indios, Native Trails, Pawprint, Portola Parkway, Prairie,\n  Prickly Pear, Ranchland, Ridge Valley, Sacred Path Seclusion, Seedling,\n  Shaman, Smallgrove, Upperbend, and WIld Trails.\n\n  5) Accept the dedication of easements for access, sidewalk, storm drain,\n  emergency access, and public service vehicle ingress and egress\n  purposes, as shown on the map.\n\n  6) Adopt a Resolution entitled: A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL\n  OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ACCEPTING THE STREETS NAMED\n  ARROWHEAD, AUTUMN SAGE, BARLEY, CANOE, CONSERVANCY\n  DEER TRACK, DISTANT STAR, EXPLORATION, GRAY DOVE,\n  JACKRABBIT, JASPER, LAND GRANT, LANDBIRD, LOS INDIOS,\n  NATIVE TRAILS, PAWPRINT, PORTOLA PARKWAY, PRAIRIE,\n  PRICKLY PEAR, RANCHLAND, RIDGE VALLEY, SACRED PATH,\n  SECLUSION, SEEDLING, SHAMAN, SMALLGROVE, UPPERBEND, AND\n  WILD TRAILS, WITHIN TRACT MAP NO. 16779 INTO THE SYSTEM OF\n  CITY STREETS\n\n  3.3 APPROVAL OF MAP, BONDS, AND AGREEMENTS FOR TRACT MAP NO.\n  16780 (A PORTION OF VESTING TENTATIVE TRACT MAP NO. 16562)\n  (PLANNING AREA 6, PORTOLA SPRINGS) (Submitted by Public\n  Works/Development Engineering)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Approve Tract Map No. 16780.\n\n  2) Approve the agreement and accept the security from Irvine Community\n  Development Company LLC and California Pacific Homes, L.P.,\n  guaranteeing improvements for Tract Map No. 16780.\n\n  3) Authorize the Mayor to sign the agreement and the City Clerk to attest to\n  the agreement subject to City Attorney approval as to form.\n\n  4) Accept the dedication of an easement for public street and public utility\n  purposes within Tract Map No. 16780 for the following street right-of-way:\n  Bell Chime, Bridge Trail, Cienega, Equinox, Full Moon, Habitat, Homeland,\n  Irvine Boulevard, Keepsake, Long Grass, Modjeska, Pathway, Portola\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  4\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n  Parkway, Portola Springs, Ridge Valley, Scarlet Bloom, Silverado, Tree\n  Clover, and White Sage.\n\n  5) Accept the dedication of easements for access, sidewalk, storm drains,\n  emergency access, and public service vehicle ingress and egress\n  purposes, as shown on the map.\n\n  6) Adopt a Resolution entitled: A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL\n  OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ACCEPTING THE STREETS NAMED BELL\n  CHIME, BRIDGE TRAIL, CIENEGA, EQUINOX, FULL MOON, HABITAT,\n  HOMELAND, IRVINE BOULEVARD, KEEPSAKE, LONG GRASS,\n  MODJESKA, PATHWAY, PORTOLA PARKWAY, PORTOLA SPRINGS,\n  RIDGE VALLEY, SCARLET BLOOM, SILVERADO, TREE CLOVER, AND\n  WHITE SAGE, WITHIN TRACT MAP NO. 16780 INTO THE SYSTEM OF\n  CITY STREETS\n\n  3.4 APPROVAL OF MAP, BONDS, AND AGREEMENTS FOR TRACT MAP NO.\n  16590 (ALL OF TENTATIVE TRACT MAP NO. 16590)(PLANNING AREA\n  36, IRVINE BUSINESS COMPLEX) (Submitted by Public\n  Works/Development Engineering)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Approve Tract Map No. 16590.\n\n  2) Approve the agreements and accept the security from Lennar KFPLB,\n  LLC, guaranteeing improvements for Tract Map No. 16590.\n\n  3) Authorize the Mayor to sign the agreements and the City Clerk to attest to\n  the agreements subject to City Attorney approval as to form.\n\n  4) Accept the dedication of an easement for public street and public utility\n  purposes within Tract Map No. 16590 for the following street right-of-way:\n  Michelson Drive and Jamboree Road.\n\n  5) Accept the dedication of easements for public trail and emergency access\n  and public service vehicle ingress and egress purposes as shown on the\n  map.\n\n  6) Accept the vehicular access rights to Jamboree Road and Michelson Drive\n  as released and relinquished as shown on the map.\n\n  7) Adopt a Resolution entitled: A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL\n  OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ACCEPTING THE STREETS NAMED\n  MICHELSON DRIVE AND JAMBOREE ROAD, WITHIN TRACT MAP NO.\n  16590 INTO THE SYSTEM OF CITY STREETS\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  5\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n  3.5 FIFTH AMENDMENT TO THE SECOND AMENDED AND RESTATED\n  JOINT POWERS AGREEMENT CREATING THE EL TORO REUSE\n  PLANNING AUTHORITY (Submitted by City Manager's Office/ACM)\n\n  ACTION:  Authorize the Mayor to sign the agreement and the City\n  Clerk to attest to the Joint Powers Agreement on behalf of the City, subject\n  to the approval of the City Attorney.\n\n  3.6 APPROVE AN AGREEMENT WITH RUTAN AND TUCKER FOR LEGAL\n  SERVICES (Submitted by City Manager's Office)\n\n  ACTION:  Approved the agreement and authorize the Mayor to execute\n  and the City clerk to attest the agreement.\n\n  3.7  AGREEMENT REGARDING HOMELESS ASSISTANCE PROVIDERS\n  LOCATED IN THE INSTITUTIONAL PARCEL AT THE ORANGE COUNTY\n  GREAT PARK (Submitted by City Manager's Office)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Direct staff to prepare an agreement with the Homeless Assistance\n  Providers (The Council of OC Society of St. Vincent de Paul, the\n  Community Action Partnership, Families Forward, and the Salvation\n  Army), Heritage Fields, LLC, the County of Orange, and/or other parties as\n  appropriate regarding the use of warehouse facilities in the Institutional\n  Parcel of the Orange County Great Park.\n\n  2) Authorize the Mayor to sign the agreement and the City Clerk to attest to\n  the agreement subject to City Attorney approval as to form.\n\n  3.8 REQUEST BY Z WEST AMERICA CORPORATION FOR THE CITY\n  COUNCIL TO DENY ASSIGNMENT OF CRESCENT IRVINE, LLC TO BE A\n  PARTY TO THE APPROVED DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT (00032520-\n  PDA)(Submitted by Community Development/Development Services)\n\n  ACTION:  Adopt a resolution entitled: A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY\n  COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE DENYING THE ASSIGNMENT OF\n  THE EXISTING DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT BY AND BETWEEN THE\n  CITY OF IRVINE AND Z WEST AMERICA CORPORATION TO\n  CRESCENT IRVINE, LLC FOR THE KOLL CENTER IRVINE\n  DEVELOPMENT LOCATED AT 1850 VON KARMAN\n\n4.PROJECTS - BIDS AND SPECIFICATIONS\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  6\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n  4.1 FY 2004/2005 REHABILITATION OF PARKING LOTS - APPROVAL OF\n  SPECIFICATIONS AND CONTRACT DOCUMENTS - CIP 365000\n  (Submitted by Public Works/Project Management)\n\n  ACTION:  Approve the specifications and contract documents for FY\n  2004/05 Rehabilitation of Parking Lots, CIP 365000.\n\n  4.2 CAMPUS DRIVE STREETSCAPE LANDSCAPE REHABILITATION FROM\n  TURTLE ROCK DRIVE TO CULVER DRIVE - APPROVAL OF PLANS,\n  SPECIFICATIONS, AND CONTRACT DOCUMENTS - CIP 354220.2\n  (Submitted by Public Works/Project Management)\n\n  ACTION:  Approve the plans, specifications, and contract documents\n  for Campus Drive Streetscape Landscape Rehabilitation from Turtle Rock\n  Drive to Culver Drive, CIP 354220.2.\n\n  4.3 ROCKVIEW AND VALLEYVIEW STREETSCAPE LANDSCAPE\n  REHABILITATION - APPROVAL OF PLANS, SPECIFICATIONS, AND\n  CONTRACT DOCUMENTS - CIP 354220.3 (Submitted by Public\n  Works/Project Management)\n\n  ACTION:  Approve the plans, specifications, and contract documents\n  for Rockview and Valleyview Streetscape Landscape Rehabilitation - CIP\n  354220.3.\n\n  4.4 EL CAMINO STREETSCAPE LANDSCAPE REHABILITATION ON IRVINE\n  CENTER DRIVE FROM CULVER DRIVE TO YALE - APPROVAL OF\n  PLANS, SPECIFICATIONS, AND CONTRACT DOCUMENTS - CIP 330510\n  (Submitted by Public Works/Project Management)\n\n  ACTION:  Approve the plans, specifications, and contract documents\n  for El Camino Streetscape Landscape Rehabilitation on Irvine Center\n  Drive from Culver Drive to Yale, CIP 330510.\n\n  4.5 BREN NEIGHBORHOOD PARK LANDSCAPE REHABILITATION -\n  APPROVAL OF PLANS, SPECIFICATIONS, AND CONTRACT\n  DOCUMENTS - CIP 384020.1 (Submitted by Public Works/Project\n  Management)\n\n  ACTION:  Approve the plans, specifications, and contract documents\n  for Bren Neighborhood Park Landscape Rehabilitation, CIP 384020.1.\n\n  4.6 AUTHORIZATION TO ADVERTISE FOR BIDS FOR LEGAL ADVERTISING\n  – FISCAL YEAR 2005-06 (Submitted by City Clerk)\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  7\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n  ACTION:  Authorize the City Clerk to advertise for bids for publication\n  of legal notices for fiscal year 2005-2006.\n\n5.RESOLUTIONS\n\n  5.1 WARRANT AND WIRE TRANSFER RESOLUTION (Submitted by\n  Administrative Services/Fiscal Services)\n\n  ACTION:  Adopt a Resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. - A\n  RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE\n  ALLOWING CERTAIN CLAIMS AND DEMANDS AND SPECIFYING THE\n  FUNDS OUT OF WHICH THE SAME ARE TO BE PAID.\n\nEND OF CONSENT CALENDAR\n\n*****************************************ORDINANCES*****************************************\n\n6.SECOND READING OF ORDINANCES\n\n  6.1 ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE,\n  CALIFORNIA, CREATING SECTION 5-9-601 THROUGH 5-9-606 OF THE\n  IRVINE MUNICIPAL CODE, REGARDING PUBLIC SAFETY RADIO\n  SYSTEM COVERAGE (Submitted by City Clerk)\n\n  ACTION:  Adopt and read by title only, an ordinance entitled:\n  ORDINANCE NO. 05-09 - AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF\n  THE CITY OF IRVINE, CALIFORNIA, CREATING SECTION 5-9-601\n  THROUGH 5-9-606 OF THE IRVINE MUNICIPAL CODE, REGARDING\n  PUBLIC SAFETY RADIO SYSTEM COVERAGE\n\n**************************************PUBLIC HEARINGS**************************************\n\n7.PUBLIC HEARING: WIRELESS COMMUNICATIONS ORDINANCE (Submitted by\n  Community Development/Development Services) (Continued from March 8,\n  2005)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Reopen public hearing.\n\n  2) Continue the public hearing until June 14, 2005.\n\n8.PUBLIC HEARING: AFFORDABLE HOUSING IN-LIEU FEE INCREASE/ANNUAL\n  ADJUSTMENT (Submitted by Community Development/Planning Services)\n\n  ACTION:\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  8\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n  1) Open public hearing.\n\n  2) Receive staff report.\n\n  3) Receive public input.\n\n  4) City Council comments and questions.\n\n  5) Close public hearing.\n\n  6) Adopt a Resolution entitled: A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL\n  OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING AN INCREASE TO THE\n  AFFORDABLE HOUSING IN-LIEU FEE\n\n9.PUBLIC HEARING: AN AMENDMENT TO THE DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT\n  FOR THE ORANGE COUNTY GREAT PARK (PLANNING AREAS 30 AND 51)\n  (Submitted by Great Park/Manager of Planning)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Open public hearing.\n\n  2) Receive staff report.\n\n  3) Receive public input.\n\n  4) Council discussion and questions.\n\n  5) Close public hearing.\n\n  6) Introduce for first reading and read by title only and ordinance entitled: AN\n  ORDINANCE OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING AN AMENDMENT\n  TO THE DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT FOR THE ORANGE COUNTY\n  GREAT PARK (PLANNING AREAS 30 AND 51)\n\n10. PUBLIC HEARING: APPEAL OF THE MARINERS CHURCH ICON SIGN\n  (Submitted by Community Development/Development Services)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Reopen public hearing.\n\n  2) Receive staff report.\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  9\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n  3) Receive public input.\n\n  4) Council comments and questions.\n\n  5) Close public hearing.\n\n  6) Adopt a resolution entitled:\n\n  A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE\n  GRANTING AN APPEAL THEREBY REVERSING THE PLANNING\n  COMMISSION’S DECISION TO DENY SIGN PROGRAM 00373941-PSS\n  FOR A 47-FOOT TALL INTERNALLY ILLUMINATED CROSS (ICON\n  SIGN) AT MARINERS CHURCH IN PLANNING AREA 27\n\n  OR\n\n  A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE\n  DENYING AN APPEAL THEREBY UPHOLDING THE PLANNING\n  COMMISSION’S DECISION TO DENY SIGN PROGRAM 00373941-PSS\n  FOR A 47-FOOT TALL INTERNALLY ILLUMINATED CROSS (ICON\n  SIGN) AT MARINERS CHURCH IN PLANNING AREA 27\n\n11. PUBLIC HEARING: CONSOLIDATED PLAN FOR FISCAL YEARS 2005-2009\n  (Continued from April 26, 2005)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Reopen public hearing.\n\n  2) Receive staff report.\n\n  3) Receive public input.\n\n  4) Council discussion and questions.\n\n  5) Close public hearing.\n\n  6) Adopt a resolution entitled: A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF\n  THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING THE CONSOLIDATED PLAN FOR\n  FISCAL YEARS 2005-2009, INCLUDING THE ONE YEAR ACTION PLAN\n  FOR FY 2005-2006, AND THE PROJECTED USE OF COMMUNITY\n  DEVELOPMENT BLOCK GRANT (CDBG), HOME INVESTMENT\n  PARTNERSHIP PROGRAM (HOME) AND AMERICAN DREAM DOWN\n  PAYMENT INITIATIVE (ADDI) FUNDS\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  10\n\fCity Council Agenda  May 10, 2005\n\n*PUBLIC COMMENTS (Limited to three (3) minutes per speaker)\n\nIN MEMORIAM\n\nAdjourn in memory of Therese Jane Francke.\n\nADJOURNMENT\n\n  Adjourn to a CITY COUNCIL REGULAR meeting, May 24, 2005, 4:00 p.m., City\n  of Irvine, City Council Chamber, One Civic Center Plaza, Irvine, California.\n\n  NOTICE TO THE PUBLIC\n\n  The foregoing does constitute the final agenda.\n\n  The agenda is available through our FAX LIBRARY system. Simply dial\n  (949)724-6210 and request document number 100 anytime after 5:00\n  p.m., on the Friday prior to a City Council meeting. The agenda may also\n  be accessed through the City’s Web page at www.ci.irvine.ca.us\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  11","minutes_text":"��\u0011ࡱ\u001a�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000>\u0000\u0003\u0000�� \u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000����\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������