\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000am\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00166\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�5\u0000\u0000\f\u0000\u0000\u0000�?Y\u000e/Z�\u0001�\b\u0000\u0000\u0004,\u0000\u0000�4\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000c7\u0000\u0000\u000e\u0002\u0000\u0000ek\u0000\u0000J\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000am\u0000\u0000�\u0002\u0000\u0000&y\u0000\u00000\u0000\u0000\u0000Vy\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�k\u0000\u0000�\u0001\u0000\u0000n}\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000q9\u0000\u0000b\u0002\u0000\u0000n}\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000am\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�;\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0006\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0007\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000d\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000d\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000d\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000d\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000M I N U T E S\r\rIRVINE\rCITY COUNCIL REGULAR MEETING\r\rMay 10, 2005\r\r\r\fCALL TO ORDER \r\rMayor Krom, presiding officer, called a regular meeting of the Irvine City Council to order on May 10, 2005 at 4:01 p.m., in the City Council Chamber, Irvine Civic Center, One Civic Center Plaza, Irvine, California.\r\rROLL CALL\r \rPRESENT:\u00075\u0007COUNCILMEMBER:\u0007Larry Agran\u0007\u0007\u0007\u0007COUNCILMEMBER:\u0007Steven Choi\u0007\u0007\u0007\u0007COUNCILMEMBER:\u0007Christina Shea\u0007\u0007\u0007\u0007MAYOR PRO TEM:\u0007Sukhee Kang \u0007\u0007\u0007\u0007MAYOR:\u0007Beth Krom\r\u0007\u0007ABSENT:\u00070\u0007COUNCILMEMBER\u0007None\u0007\u0007\rAlso present were City Manager, Allison Hart; Assistant City Manager, Sean Joyce; Assistant City Manager Wally Kreutzen; City Attorney, Joel Kuperberg; Director of Public Safety, David L. Maggard, Director of Administrative Services, Rick Paikoff; Director of Public Works, Marty Bryant; Acting Director of Community Services, John McAllister; Director of Community Development, Tina Christiansen; City Clerk, Jeri Stately; Deputy City Clerk, Teri Beach; and Sergeant At Arms, Michael Tu.\r\r\rRECESS\r\rMayor Krom recessed the City Council meeting to the Irvine Redevelopment Agency meeting at 4:02 p.m.\r\r\rCONVENE TO THE IRVINE REDEVELOPMENT AGENCY MEETING\r\rMayor Krom convened a meeting of the Irvine Redevelopment Agency meeting at 4:02 p.m.\r\rPlease see Irvine Redevelopment Agency minutes.\r\r\rRECONVENE TO THE CITY COUNCIL MEETING \r\rMayor Krom reconvened the City Council meeting at 4:05 p.m.\r\r\rPRESENTATIONS/SCOPING SESSIONS\r\rPRESENTATION: TUSTIN UNIFIED SCHOOL DISTRICT �\r\rMayor Krom introduced Superintendent Peter C. Gorman, Ed. D., Lynn Davis, Board Member - Tustin Unified School District; and Francine Scinto, President - Tustin Unified School District. President Scinto and Superintendent Gorman gave a brief presentation on the school structure in the City of Tustin. (Exhibit No. 1 on file in the City Clerk�s Department.)\r\rCity Council discussion included school district boundaries and challenges facing both Irvine and Tustin Cities in the planning process. \r\rNo action was taken on this item.\r\r\rSCOPING SESSION: PLANNING AREAS 1, 2, AND 9B (Submitted by Community Development/Planning Services)\r\rBarry Curtis, Principal Planner briefly introduced the item. Mike Le Blanc and Roger McErlane, representing The Irvine Company, presented details of the upcoming project. (Exhibit No. 2 on file in the City Clerk�s Department.) \r\r David Melvold, Irvine resident, spoke on the electrical sub station that will be constructed by the Southern California Edison at the proposed project site. (Exhibit No. 4 on file in the City Clerk�s Department.) \r\rNo action was taken on this item.\r\r\rRECESS\r\rMayor Krom recessed the City Council meeting at 4:53 p.m.\r\r\rRECONVENE TO THE CITY COUNCIL MEETING\r\rMayor Krom reconvened the City Council meeting at 5:19 p.m.\r\rPLEDGE OF ALLEGIANCE\r\rMayor Pro Tempore Kang led the Pledge of Allegiance.\r\r\rMOMENT OF SILENCE\r\rMayor Krom noted the City Council meeting would be adjourned in memory of Therese Jane Francke.\r\r\rMUSICAL PRESENTATION\r\rMayor Krom introduced the University High School Sax Quartet who performed \"Luxury Lane\" by Carl Frangkiser and the Clarinet Quartet who performed \"Chicago\" by Fred Fisher.\r\r\rPRESENTATIONS\r\r1) Mayor Krom introduced members (listed below) of the Public Works Department and presented a proclamation to Manual Gomez, Deputy Director of Public Works, honoring �National Public Works Week - May 15-21, 2005.� (A video was shown and is hereto referenced as Exhibit No. 3.)\r\r Rudy Romo, Associate Engineer/Development Engineering;\r Billy Walker, Street Maintenance Technician;\r John Dupont, Street Maintenance Supervisor;\r Dennis Chiotti, Landscape Maintenance Supervisor;\r Virginia Kean, Administrative Secretary/Administration;\r Manual Gomez, Deputy Director of Public Works; and\r Darrell Hartman, Senior Civil Engineer/Project Management.\r\r2) Mayor Krom introduced Duane Cave, South Orange County Regional Chamber of Commerce who presented the City Council with the �Regional Cities Crystal Ball.�\r\r3) Mayor Krom introduced Joanne Slobodien, representing the American Cancer Society, spoke on the Relay for Life Event, to be held on Saturday, May 21 to Sunday, May 22, from 10:00 a.m. to 10:00 a.m. at Irvine Valley College.\r\rINTRODUCTIONS\r\rCouncilmember Agran made the following introductions:\rCameron Cosgrove � Planning Commissioner, not present;\rDr. Omar Ezzeldine � Finance Commissioner;\rMariam Khosravani � Community Services Commissioner;\rGenet Gomez � Child Care Committee;\rNajma Quader � Senior Council; \rLucy Walther � Investment Advisory Committee;\rSubia Aleem � Executive Assistant;\rLori Ballard � Executive Assistant; not present;\rKathy Graves � Executive Assistant; and\rMary King � Executive Assistant.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/COMMITTEE REPORTS/COUNCIL REPORTS\r\rMayor Krom made the following announcements:\rIrvine will be conducting its second annual photo contest, �Only in Irvine Photo Contest.� She noted amateur photographers of all ages are invited to participate, and the deadline for submissions is May 31, 2005. Winning photos will be showcased on the City�s Website, and Irvine Community Television Channel 30;\rThe Irvine Global Village Festival will be held on Saturday, June 11, 12:00 to 5:00 p.m., at Colonel Bill Barber Marine Corps Memorial Park;\rThe Irvine Fine Arts Center, in collaboration with the Legacy Project and the Great Park Corporation, will host the �Edge of Air: An Exhibition of Photography of the Final Days of the Marine Corps Air Station at El Toro.� The public is invited to attend the artist reception on Sunday, June 12, from 6:00 to 8:00 p.m. at the Irvine Fine Arts Center. The exhibition will be on display through July 16;\rThe Irvine Fine Arts Center will host its annual fundraiser, the Studio Arts Festival, on Saturday, June 4, from 9:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.;\rThe Irvine Public Schools Foundation will have its 2nd annual house raffle. Tickets are currently being sold and she noted that ticket sales have been extended one week to May 20; and\rAn out-going reception for City Manager Allison Hart will be held on May 24, 2005 from 4:00 � 5:00 p.m. in the Conference and Training Center.\r\rMayor Pro Tempore Kang made the following announcements:\rHe attended a meeting with Marlan Gloverson, Lesley Bindloss, Coach Charles Gates, Mike LeBlanc, John Graves, Sharon Heider, and Subia Aleem, regarding community access to the Northern Open Space; he acknowledged The Irvine Company and Acting Director of Community Services John McAllister and staff for assisting in providing access to the trail; and\rDr. Kevin Lance Armstrong, a graduate of Woodbridge High School, a successful orthopedic surgeon and professor at UCI Medical Center, passed away suddenly on Tuesday, May 3; funeral services will be held on Wednesday, May 11, from 10:00 a.m. to noon at Mariners Church.\r\r\rPUBLIC COMMENTS \r\rDave Melvold, Irvine resident, spoke on the library construction fund and the need to consider another library within the City limits.\r\rVirginia Read, Irvine resident, spoke on the City�s hiring procedures and her meeting with Rick Paikoff, Director of Administrative Services.\r\rLaurie Truman, Irvine resident, spoke on the convenience store/gas station proposed to be located in the Quail Hill area and noted incompatibility of uses associated with this location.\r\r\rADDITIONS AND DELETIONS\r\rCity Manager Allison Hart noted the deletion of Item No. 3.8 from the agenda, �Request by Z West America Corporation for City Council Approval of Assignment Of Crescent Irvine, LLC to be a Party to the Approved Development Agreement (00032520-PDA).� She stated that this item will be re-agendized for the meeting of May 24.\r\r\rCONSENT CALENDAR \r\r\rACTION: With the exception of Item No. 3.8, as noted in �Additions and Deletions,� it was moved by Councilmember Choi, seconded by Councilmember Shea, and unanimously carried to approve Consent Calendar Item Nos. 1 through 5.1. \r\rPUBLIC COMMENTS \r\rThere was no public comment on Consent Calendar items. \r\r\rCITY COUNCIL MINUTES\r\rAPPROVAL OF CITY COUNCIL MINUTES (Submitted by City Clerk)\r\rACTION: Approved the minutes of a special meeting of the City Council held on April 26, 2005.\r\r\rPROCLAMATIONS/COMMENDATIONS/RATIFICATIONS\r\rPROCLAIMED THE FOLLOWING:\u000b\u000b1) Taiwanese American Heritage Week - May 16-22, 2005.\r\u000b2) National Public Works Week - May 15-21, 2005\u000b\rCOMMENDED THE FOLLOWING:\u000b\r1) Ralph J. Cicerone, Retiring Chancellor, University of California, Irvine, 1998-2005\r\r\rAGREEMENTS\r\rRENEW LICENSE AGREEMENT WITH SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA EDISON FOR BIKE TRAIL/PEDESTRIAN ACCESS AND LANDSCAPING PURPOSES, WEST OF SAND CANYON AVENUE, NORTH OF BARRANCA PARKWAY (PLANNING AREA 12, OAK CREEK) (Submitted by Public Works/Development Engineering)\r\rACTION: CONTRACT NO. 3896A - Approved License Agreement Account Number 2217 between the City of Irvine and Southern California Edison, and authorized the Mayor to execute and the City Clerk to attest said agreement, subject to the City Attorney approval as to form.\r\rAPPROVAL OF MAP, BONDS, AND AGREEMENTS FOR TRACT MAP NO. 16779 (A PORTION OF VESTING TENTATIVE TRACT MAP NO. 16562) (PLANNING AREA 6, PORTOLA SPRINGS) (Submitted by Public Works/Development Engineering)\r\rACTION:\rApproved Tract Map No. 16779.\r\rApproved the agreements and accepted the security from Pardee Homes, Irvine Community Development Company LLC, and Standard Pacific Corporation, guaranteeing improvements for Tract Map No. 16779.\r\rAuthorized the Mayor to sign the agreements and the City Clerk to attest to the agreements subject to City Attorney approval as to form.\r\rAccepted the dedication of an easement for public street and public utility purposes within Tract Map No. 16779 for the following street right-of-way: Arrowhead, Autumn Sage, Barley, Canoe, Conservancy, Deer Track, Distant Star, Exploration, Gray Dove, Jackrabbit, Jasper, Land Grant, Landbird, Los Indios, Native Trails, Pawprint, Portola Parkway, Prairie, Prickly Pear, Ranchland, Ridge Valley, Sacred Path Seclusion, Seedling, Shaman, Smallgrove, Upperbend, and Wild Trails.\r\rAccepted the dedication of easements for access, sidewalk, storm drain, emergency access, and public service vehicle ingress and egress purposes, as shown on the map.\r\rAdopt a Resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-46 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ACCEPTING THE STREETS NAMED ARROWHEAD, AUTUMN SAGE, BARLEY, CANOE, CONSERVANCY DEER TRACK, DISTANT STAR, EXPLORATION, GRAY DOVE, JACKRABBIT, JASPER, LAND GRANT, LANDBIRD, LOS INDIOS, NATIVE TRAILS, PAWPRINT, PORTOLA PARKWAY, PRAIRIE, PRICKLY PEAR, RANCHLAND, RIDGE VALLEY, SACRED PATH, SECLUSION, SEEDLING, SHAMAN, SMALLGROVE, UPPERBEND, AND WILD TRAILS, WITHIN TRACT MAP NO. 16779 INTO THE SYSTEM OF CITY STREETS\r\r\rAPPROVAL OF MAP, BONDS, AND AGREEMENTS FOR TRACT MAP NO. 16780 (A PORTION OF VESTING TENTATIVE TRACT MAP NO. 16562) (PLANNING AREA 6, PORTOLA SPRINGS) (Submitted by Public Works/Development Engineering)\r\rACTION:\rApproved Tract Map No. 16780.\r\rApproved the agreement and accepted the security from Irvine Community Development Company LLC and California Pacific Homes, L.P., guaranteeing improvements for Tract Map No. 16780.\r\rAuthorized the Mayor to sign the agreement and the City Clerk to attest to the agreement subject to City Attorney approval as to form.\r\rAccepted the dedication of an easement for public street and public utility purposes within Tract Map No. 16780 for the following street right-of-way: Bell Chime, Bridge Trail, Cienega, Equinox, Full Moon, Habitat, Homeland, Irvine Boulevard, Keepsake, Long Grass, Modjeska, Pathway, Portola Parkway, Portola Springs, Ridge Valley, Scarlet Bloom, Silverado, Tree Clover, and White Sage.\r\rAccepted the dedication of easements for access, sidewalk, storm drains, emergency access, and public service vehicle ingress and egress purposes, as shown on the map.\r\r\r\r\rAdopted a Resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-47 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ACCEPTING THE STREETS NAMED BELL CHIME, BRIDGE TRAIL, CIENEGA, EQUINOX, FULL MOON, HABITAT, HOMELAND, IRVINE BOULEVARD, KEEPSAKE, LONG GRASS, MODJESKA, PATHWAY, PORTOLA PARKWAY, PORTOLA SPRINGS, RIDGE VALLEY, SCARLET BLOOM, SILVERADO, TREE CLOVER, AND WHITE SAGE, WITHIN TRACT MAP NO. 16780 INTO THE SYSTEM OF CITY STREETS\r\r\rAPPROVAL OF MAP, BONDS, AND AGREEMENTS FOR TRACT MAP NO. 16590 (ALL OF TENTATIVE TRACT MAP NO. 16590)(PLANNING AREA 36, IRVINE BUSINESS COMPLEX) (Submitted by Public Works/Development Engineering)\r\rACTION:\rApproved Tract Map No. 16590.\r\rApproved the agreements and accepted the security from Lennar KFPLB, LLC, guaranteeing improvements for Tract Map No. 16590. \r\rAuthorized the Mayor to sign the agreements and the City Clerk to attest to the agreements subject to City Attorney approval as to form.\r\rAccepted the dedication of an easement for public street and public utility purposes within Tract Map No. 16590 for the following street right-of-way: Michelson Drive and Jamboree Road.\r\rAccepted the dedication of easements for public trail and emergency access and public service vehicle ingress and egress purposes as shown on the map. \r\rAccepted the vehicular access rights to Jamboree Road and Michelson Drive as released and relinquished as shown on the map. \r\rAdopted a Resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-48 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ACCEPTING THE STREETS NAMED MICHELSON DRIVE AND JAMBOREE ROAD, WITHIN TRACT MAP NO. 16590 INTO THE SYSTEM OF CITY STREETS\r\r\r\rFIFTH AMENDMENT TO THE SECOND AMENDED AND RESTATED JOINT POWERS AGREEMENT CREATING THE EL TORO REUSE PLANNING AUTHORITY (Submitted by City Manager's Office/ACM)\r\rThis item was removed from the Consent Calendar at the request of Councilmember Shea who had questions related to maintaining the City�s position on the El Toro Reuse Planning Authority; and clarification of the Authority�s role since the sale of the Great Park; to which Dan Jung, Executive Assistant to the City Manager.\r\rACTION: It was moved by Councilmember Shea, seconded by Mayor Krom and unanimously carried, to: \r\rCONTRACT NO. 3007H - Authorize the Mayor to sign the agreement and the City Clerk to attest to the Joint Powers Agreement on behalf of the City, subject to the approval of the City Attorney.\r\r\rAPPROVE AN AGREEMENT WITH RUTAN AND TUCKER FOR LEGAL SERVICES (Submitted by City Manager's Office)\r\rACTION: CONTRACT NO. 5008 - Approved the agreement and authorized