BILITATION - APPROVAL OF PLANS, SPECIFICATIONS, AND CONTRACT DOCUMENTS - CIP 354220.3 (Submitted by Public Works/Project Management)\r\rACTION: Approved the plans, specifications, and contract documents for Rockview and Valleyview Streetscape Landscape Rehabilitation - CIP 354220.3.\r\rEL CAMINO STREETSCAPE LANDSCAPE REHABILITATION ON IRVINE CENTER DRIVE FROM CULVER DRIVE TO YALE - APPROVAL OF PLANS, SPECIFICATIONS, AND CONTRACT DOCUMENTS - CIP 330510 (Submitted by Public Works/Project Management)\r\rACTION: Approved the plans, specifications, and contract documents for El Camino Streetscape Landscape Rehabilitation on Irvine Center Drive from Culver Drive to Yale, CIP 330510.\r\rBREN NEIGHBORHOOD PARK LANDSCAPE REHABILITATION - APPROVAL OF PLANS, SPECIFICATIONS, AND CONTRACT DOCUMENTS - CIP 384020.1 (Submitted by Public Works/Project Management)\r\rACTION: Approved the plans, specifications, and contract documents for Bren Neighborhood Park Landscape Rehabilitation, CIP 384020.1.\r\r\rAUTHORIZATION TO ADVERTISE FOR BIDS FOR LEGAL ADVERTISING � FISCAL YEAR 2005-06 (Submitted by City Clerk)\r\rACTION: Authorized the City Clerk to advertise for bids for publication of legal notices for fiscal year 2005-2006.\r\r\rRESOLUTIONS\r\rWARRANT AND WIRE TRANSFER RESOLUTION (Submitted by Administrative Services/Fiscal Services)\r\rACTION: Adopted a resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-49 RESOLUTION NO. - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ALLOWING CERTAIN CLAIMS AND DEMANDS AND SPECIFYING THE FUNDS OUT OF WHICH THE SAME ARE TO BE PAID.\r\rEND OF CONSENT CALENDAR\r\rORDINANCES\r\rSECOND READING OF ORDINANCES\r\rORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE, CALIFORNIA, CREATING SECTION 5-9-601 THROUGH 5-9-606 OF THE IRVINE MUNICIPAL CODE, REGARDING PUBLIC SAFETY RADIO SYSTEM COVERAGE (Submitted by City Clerk)\r\rACTION: It was moved by Councilmember Shea, seconded by Mayor Pro Tempore Kang, and unanimously carried, to:\r\rAdopt and read by title only, an ordinance entitled: ORDINANCE NO. 05-09 - AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE, CALIFORNIA, CREATING SECTION 5-9-601 THROUGH 5-9-606 OF THE IRVINE MUNICIPAL CODE, REGARDING PUBLIC SAFETY RADIO SYSTEM COVERAGE\r\rPUBLIC HEARINGS\r\rPUBLIC HEARING: WIRELESS COMMUNICATIONS ORDINANCE (Submitted by Community Development/Development Services) (Continued from March 8, 2005)\r\rMayor Krom declared the public hearing re-opened at 6:42 p.m.\r\r\rACTION: At 6:42, it was moved by Councilmember Agran, seconded by Mayor Krom, and unanimously carried, to:\r\rContinue the public hearing to the meeting of June 14, 2005.\r\r\rPUBLIC HEARING: AFFORDABLE HOUSING IN-LIEU FEE INCREASE/ANNUAL ADJUSTMENT (Submitted by Community Development/Planning Services)\r\rMayor Krom declared the public hearing open at 6:43 p.m.\r\rBarry Curtis, Principal Planner, and Brian Fisk, Manager of Planning Services presented the staff report. (PowerPoint presentation and Exhibit No. 5 on file in the City Clerk�s Department.)\r\r The following individuals spoke on the process used to determine completion of applications for projects in process:\r Matt Montgomery, Opus West\r Pamela Sapetto, Sapetto Group, Inc.\r\r City Council discussion included how reductions in fees are determined; clarification of how the annual adjustment fee was initially determined; clarification of the process used to develop the fee matrix; possibility of establishing a multi-annual fee structure adjustment; clarification that annual adjustments are determined on market based data which represents the actual cost; clarification of cost to developer to pay in-lieu fees vs. cost to construct on-site; and the need for staff to return to the City Council with an analysis of the projects that have been submitted and are currently in process.\r\r ACTION: At 7:27 p.m., it was moved by Councilmember Agran, seconded by Councilmember Shea, and unanimously carried to close the public hearing.\r\r\r\r\r\rIt was moved by Councilmember Agran, seconded by Mayor Krom, to:\r\rAdopt a resolution entitled: A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING AN INCREASE TO THE AFFORDABLE HOUSING IN-LIEU FEE\r\rAs amended to delete Section 3.\r\rA substitute motion was moved by Councilmember Choi to adopt the resolution as presented to the City Council with Section 3 included. The motion failed due to lack of a second.\r\r\rACTION: It was moved by Councilmember Agran, seconded by Mayor Krom, to:\r\rAdopt a resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-50 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING AN INCREASE TO THE AFFORDABLE HOUSING IN-LIEU FEE\r\rAs amended to delete Section 3.\r\rThe original motion (as noted above) carried as follows:\r\rAYES:\u00073\u0007COUNCILMEMBERS:\u0007Agran, Kang and Krom\r\u0007\u0007NOES:\u00072\u0007COUNCILMEMBERS:\u0007Choi and Shea\r\u0007\u0007ABSENT:\u00070\u0007COUNCILMEMBERS:\u0007None\r\u0007\u0007\rCouncilmember Agran requested that staff return to the City Council by June 14:\rTo address those projects meeting the thresholds set in Section 3 of the originally proposed resolution; and \rTo provide details of increasing the frequency with which adjustments to the in-lieu fees are prepared.\r\r\rPUBLIC HEARING: AN AMENDMENT TO THE DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT FOR THE ORANGE COUNTY GREAT PARK (PLANNING AREAS 30 AND 51) (Submitted by Great Park/Manager of Planning)\r\rMayor Krom declared the public hearing open at 7:36 p.m.\r\rGlen Worthington, Planning Manager � Orange County Great Park, introduced the staff report. \r\r ACTION: At 7:37 p.m., it was moved by Councilmember Shea, seconded by Mayor Krom, and unanimously carried to close the public hearing.\r\rACTION: It was moved by Councilmember Shea, seconded by Mayor Pro Tempore Kang, and unanimously carried, to:\r\rIntroduce for first reading and read by title only and ordinance entitled: ORDINANCE NO. 05-10 - AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING AN AMENDMENT TO THE DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT FOR THE ORANGE COUNTY GREAT PARK (PLANNING AREAS 30 AND 51)\r\r\rPUBLIC HEARING: APPEAL OF THE MARINERS CHURCH ICON SIGN (Submitted by Community Development/Development Services) \r\rMayor Krom declared the public hearing open at 7:40 p.m.\r\rTrevor Lottes, Senior Planner, and Tim Gehrich, Principal Planner presented the staff report. (PowerPoint presentation on file as Exhibit No. 6 in the City Clerk�s Department.)\r\rCity Council discussion included clarification of how determination was made to change the definition of the proposed sign from an architectural sign to an icon sign; clarification that criteria used to determine definition as an icon sign was based upon neon and illumination; distance from University Hills to the Church site; clarification of the sign described as a �unique visual element�; number of services conducted weekly at Mariners� Church; clarification of the church�s plan to construct an additional Worship Center; whether illuminated crosses exist at any other church facilities in the City; whether any other concepts were considered by the church in terms of creating a unique visual element for the building other than illumination; concern with visual impact on community; clarification of permit requirements for lighting schemes; continue to conduct outreach to the neighboring community for the purpose of determining the impact of the illuminated cross on the neighborhood; and clarification of notification to the residents by Mariners Church.\r\rThe following individuals spoke in opposition to the approval of the proposed sign:\rBill Dahl, Irvine resident; (E-mail transmission and Exhibit No. 7on file in the City Clerk�s Department.)\rMs. Komal Dewan, Irvine resident;\rDr. Barbara J. Becker, Irvine resident; (E-mail transmission and Exhibit No. 8on file in the City Clerk�s Department.)\rClaudia Shambaugh, Irvine resident;\rTammy Smecker-Hane, Irvine resident; and\rMichael Szalay, Irvine resident\r\r\r The following individuals spoke in support of approval of the proposed sign:\rGloria Broming, Irvine resident;\rWes Smith, Irvine resident;\rBrian Norkaitis, Irvine resident;\rSusan DeMaggio, Irvine resident; (E-mail transmission and Exhibit No. 9on file in the City Clerk�s Department.)and\rJames Raver, Irvine resident\r \rACTION: At 9:41 p.m., it was moved by Councilmember Shea, seconded by Councilmember Choi, to close the public hearing. \r\rThe motion carried as follows:\r\rAYES:\u00073\u0007COUNCILMEMBERS:\u0007Choi, Kang, and Shea\r\u0007\u0007NOES:\u00072\u0007COUNCILMEMBERS:\u0007Agran and Krom \r\u0007\u0007ABSENT:\u00070\u0007COUNCILMEMBERS:\u0007None\r\u0007\u0007\rACTION: It was moved by Councilmember Choi, seconded by Councilmember Shea, and unanimously carried, to:\r\rAdopt a resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-51 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE GRANTING AN APPEAL THEREBY REVERSING THE PLANNING COMMISSION�S DECISION TO DENY SIGN PROGRAM 00373941-PSS FOR A 47-FOOT TALL INTERNALLY ILLUMINATED CROSS (ICON SIGN) AT MARINERS CHURCH IN PLANNING AREA 27\r\rAs amended to include the following:\r\rThe lighting is to be extinguished between 9:00 p.m. and sunset of the following day; and\rProvide that the Director of Community Development or a representative shall review the intensity of the lighting within 6 months of commencement of operation of the illuminated sign and allow the Director of Community Development or a representative the authority to introduce measures to request the applicant to reduce the intensity of the lighting accordingly, if necessary.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING: CONSOLIDATED PLAN FOR FISCAL YEARS 2005-2009 (Continued from April 26, 2005)\r\rMayor Krom declared the public hearing open at 10:32 p.m.\r\rCynthia Ricks-Maccotan, Grants Coordinator; Barry Curtis, Principal Planner, presented the staff report.\r\r ACTION: At 10:32 p.m., it was moved by Mayor Krom, seconded by Mayor Pro Tempore Kang, and unanimously carried to close the public hearing.\r\rACTION: It was moved by Mayor Krom, seconded by Mayor Pro Tempore Kang, and unanimously carried to:\r\rAdopt a resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-52 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING THE CONSOLIDATED PLAN FOR FISCAL YEARS 2005-2009, INCLUDING THE ONE YEAR ACTION PLAN FOR FY 2005-2006, AND THE PROJECTED USE OF COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT BLOCK GRANT (CDBG), HOME INVESTMENT PARTNERSHIP PROGRAM (HOME) AND AMERICAN DREAM DOWN PAYMENT INITIATIVE (ADDI) FUNDS\r\r\rIN MEMORIAM\r\rMayor Krom adjourned the meeting in memory of Therese Jane Francke.\r\r\rADJOURNMENT\r\rIt was moved by Mayor Krom, seconded by Mayor Pro Tempore Kang, and unanimously carried to adjourn the meeting at 10:34 p.m., to a City Council Regular meeting, May 24, 2005, 4:00 p.m., City of Irvine, City Council Chamber, One Civic Center Plaza, Irvine, California.\r\rNote: A reception honoring retiring City Manager Allison Hart will be held at 4:00 p.m. on May 24 in the Conference and Training Center.\r\r\r\r ________________________________\r MAYOR OF THE CITY OF IRVINE\r\r\r\r\r____________________________________ _May 24, 2005_____\rCITY CLERK OF THE CITY OF IRVINE DATE APPROVED\r\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \u00141\u0015\r\rCity Council Minutes May 10, 2005\r\r\rPrepared by the City Clerk�s Office \u0013 PAGE \u001416\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u